38. Canonical Invariants

Any implementation claiming compatibility with Pantheon Calculus should preserve these invariants.

Invariant 1 — Semantics Before Coordinates

Meaning belongs to objects and relationships, not visual placement.

Invariant 2 — Deterministic Core Where Possible

AI may interpret intent and construct computation.

Mathematics should remain independently executable and inspectable.

Invariant 3 — Pattern ≠ Cause

Pattern discovery must not silently become causal assertion.

Invariant 4 — Provenance Is Mandatory

Every significant result must be traceable.

Invariant 5 — Views Are Projections

Spreadsheet, graph, dashboard, and conversation operate on the same underlying model.

Invariant 6 — Algorithms Are Operators

Strategies have assumptions, interfaces, failure modes, and validation procedures.

Invariant 7 — Algorithms Compose

Higher-order problem solving emerges from operator composition.

Invariant 8 — Patterns Become Objects

Detected regularities can be stored, compared, tested, and composed.

Invariant 9 — Meta-Patterns Are First-Class

Relationships between patterns deserve explicit representation.

Invariant 10 — Insight Must Survive Attack

Important discoveries should be subjected to adversarial validation.

Invariant 11 — Counterfactuals Are Native

Branching and scenario exploration should not require duplicated workbooks.

Invariant 12 — The Interface Adapts to the Problem

The grid is one useful projection, not the universal computational surface.

