41. Failure Modes

Future implementations should explicitly watch for:

Semantic hallucination

Incorrectly interpreting what a variable means.

False pattern discovery

Finding statistically accidental relationships.

Causal inflation

Presenting correlation as mechanism.

Hidden assumptions

Automatically constructing a model whose assumptions the user cannot inspect.

Router opacity

Selecting methods without exposing why the method is appropriate at a high level.

Combinatorial explosion

Testing enormous numbers of pattern combinations without statistical discipline.

Interface over-automation

Changing representations so aggressively that the user loses orientation.

Optimization against the wrong objective

Finding an excellent answer to an incorrectly specified goal.

False precision

Presenting uncertainty as deterministic certainty.

Model monoculture

Repeatedly selecting familiar algorithms even when alternatives better fit the problem.

