43. North Star

The objective is not to make spreadsheet users faster at operating spreadsheets.

The objective is to make the spreadsheet disappear whenever its interface is unnecessary while preserving everything valuable about its computational model.

The ultimate interaction should feel less like programming a worksheet and more like manipulating reality’s variables:

Here is what exists.

Here is what depends on what.

Here is what changed.

Here are the patterns.

Here is what we do not understand.

Here are the available moves.

Here is what happens if we make each one.

Here is the best path under the constraints you gave me.

That is the post-spreadsheet interface.

Not a smarter calculator.

A computational instrument for seeing, manipulating, and navigating structured possibility.

A few things I would put beside that paper in the repo because they will materially help the next model reconstruct rather than merely admire the idea:

* specs/SCIR.md — the actual Semantic Computational IR schema. Make Quantity, Entity, Relationship, Constraint, Goal, Scenario, Pattern, Hypothesis, Insight, and Operator concrete types.
* specs/OPERATOR_ROUTER.md — define algorithm selection as a routing/portfolio problem, including assumptions, expected utility, fallback behavior, ensemble/composition, and validation.
* specs/PATTERN_OBSERVATORY.md — the pattern → pattern-object → meta-pattern → tested insight pipeline.
* specs/EVIDENCE_LADDER.md — lock in the distinction between “interesting resemblance,” statistical association, prediction, mechanism, and causality. This one is important because otherwise a powerful pattern engine becomes an apophenia machine.
* registry/operators.yaml — machine-readable operator catalog. The next model shouldn’t have to rediscover what Pantheon knows how to do.
* registry/patterns.yaml — known structural motifs plus provenance, domains observed, counterexamples, and confidence.
* tests/golden_cases/ — a handful of tiny examples whose correct behavior defines the architecture better than prose can. Mortgage Goal Seek, DCF, budget, hidden cohort reversal, regime change, and formula-pattern recognition would be excellent initial cases.
* RECONSTRUCTION.md — one brutally compressed document explaining what absolutely must survive if every other file disappears.

I’d also add one new operator that I think is particularly important: Thread Pull.

Its input is any surprising observation. Its job is recursively:

observation → dependencies → neighboring patterns → transformations → scales → analogous structures → competing explanations → discriminating test

But it receives an information/compute budget and stops when expected information gain drops below a threshold. That gives you a disciplined version of exactly what you described: see something interesting, pull the thread farther than a human normally would, but do not wander forever or mistake coincidence for structure.

And the deepest version of this becomes a Pattern Compiler:

raw events → deltas → patterns → meta-patterns → invariants → operators → reusable models.

That is where this stops merely being an upgraded financial tool. It starts converting repeated experience into new computational machinery.